sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, Recall analytics-plausible-via-swamp, DECISIONS 1 (cert signing), 2 (DNS hold), R2-R4. docs/reference/analytics.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:analytics:enable
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane P icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>serves the host
  participant P as Plausible<br/>analytics.orbit
  CLI->>GW: instance:analytics:enable<br/>42 --host=HOST (repeatable)
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:analytics:enable 42 --host=stats.shop.example.com`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--host=HOST]... [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Instance ID
  %%> - up to ten tracking hosts; without `--host`, `analytics.<instance domain>`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates or updates the Instance's Plausible site, and publishes the tracking hosts
  %%> - sets the exact host set: hosts you leave out are removed
  Note over GW: Validate, plan the hosts<br/>task #5126 · Instance lock
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - a Node has the active `analytics` role (`analytics.role_missing`)
  %%> - Instance 42 serves a domain (`analytics.domain_required`)
  %%> - no other Route owns a named host (`analytics.host_taken`)
  %%> - no other analytics or Route change runs for Instance 42; the Gateway holds one lock
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the site domain (the Instance's own domain), timezone and goals
  %%> - each host's tracking Route, copying the Node, Cluster and publication of the Instance's Route
  %%> - the Caddy sites, certificate requests and before state
  %%> Result:
  %%> - tracking Routes recorded as provisioning; task #5126 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Push credentials to vault<br/>analytics-plausible-5126
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the Plausible login to the Swamp vault after commit (R3)
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the workflow gets only the vault key name, never the value
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-analytics-enable
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the site, goals, hosts, Caddy sites and certificate requests
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5126
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>P: Converge the site<br/>command/shell · site.py
  %%> How:
  %%> - one shipped script logs in at `https://analytics.orbit` with the vault credentials
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates the site when it is missing, or updates it; never a duplicate
  %%> - sets the timezone and the requested goals, checks them, and logs out, also after a failure
  %%> Never:
  %%> - session cookies or tokens in outputs or files
  opt host is served by a Router
    SW->>N: Request the certificate<br/>CSR for the tracking host
    %%> When:
    %%> - only when Instance 42's Route is Cluster-scoped; then Node 12 is the Router
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - makes a key and a CSR on Node 12; the private key never leaves it
    %%> - public Ingress uses its own automatic public certificates
    SW->>GW: Sign the CSR<br/>certificate-sign primitive
    %%> Why a call to the Gateway:
    %%> - certificate signing is the one allowed step→Gateway call; the Orbit CA stays in the Gateway
    GW-->>SW: Signed certificate<br/>installed on Node 12
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the signed certificate; Swamp installs it on Node 12
  end
  SW->>N: Publish Caddy, reload<br/>/js/* and /api/event only
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - adds a site per host that proxies only Plausible's script and event paths over WireGuard; every other path answers 404
  %%> - removes sites of hosts you left out; validates, then reloads Caddy without a restart
  SW->>N: Probe the tracking host<br/>TLS · GET /js/script.js
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks the host answers with a valid certificate and serves the script
  Note over SW: Publish private DNS<br/>open: Nick decides (DNS hold)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - publishes the hosts' private DNS records, waits the 31-second grace, then withdraws old placements
  %%> Open:
  %%> - the DNS hold (`native-dns-takeover-held`) is in force; Nick decides how Route DNS is published
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - the public CNAME; `instance:analytics:show` names the record to create
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Tracking Routes active<br/>site binding · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the tracking Routes become active; removed hosts' Routes are deleted
    %%> - the Plausible site binding is saved; task #5126 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or probe fails
    %%> When:
    %%> - the Plausible call, a certificate, Caddy or the probe fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its public error code; never a Plausible response body
    Note over GW: Mark the Routes failed<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the tracking Routes stay, marked failed; task #5126 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a Plausible site already created stays; a rerun finds and reuses it
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it converges the same site and hosts
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5126
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
